Make status an enum and allow changes only through a guarded setter (or a `transition_to` method) that checks a table of allowed transitions.

```python
ALLOWED = {PENDING: {PAID, CANCELLED}, PAID: {SHIPPED, CANCELLED}, SHIPPED: set(), CANCELLED: set()}

@status.setter
def status(self, new: OrderStatus) -> None:
    if new not in ALLOWED[self._status]:
        raise ValueError(...)
    self._status = new
```

Invalid transitions now fail loudly at the point of the bug.
